If there is metadata that should apply to the entire application (for example, a default title, description, or favicon), you can define it in the root layout.js or layout.tsx file inside the app folder.

For pages that need their own specific metadata, you can export a metadata object directly from that page file.

Example:

export const metadata = {
  title: 'Meals Page',
  description: 'Browse delicious meals',
};

Important:

Page-level metadata overrides root layout metadata when both define the same property.
Any metadata properties not defined on the page are inherited from the parent layout metadata.

So Next.js merges metadata hierarchically, with more specific metadata taking precedence.

